WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.749
AI writes code faster than ever.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.085
According to DORA 2025 and 2026,

00:00:06.085 --> 00:00:08.288
it speeds up delivery,

00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:11.182
but also increases instability.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.019
Kaizen turns Claude Code into a

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:14.961
controlled development cycle.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.374
Everything starts from a

00:00:16.374 --> 00:00:18.337
constitution: your principles,

00:00:18.337 --> 00:00:20.305
each with a verifiable check.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.913
The brainstorm defines
what to build.

00:00:23.913 --> 00:00:25.376
The plan decides how.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.472
Requirements, tests,

00:00:28.472 --> 00:00:30.545
rollback: everything is traced,

00:00:30.545 --> 00:00:32.869
then reviewed by
specialized agents.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.781
During the work, a
quality gate blocks the

00:00:37.781 --> 00:00:39.896
end of a step while
tests are red.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.661
Reviewers chosen for
the changed code

00:00:43.661 --> 00:00:45.363
inspect it, and without their

00:00:45.363 --> 00:00:47.136
review, nothing is pushed.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.560
The PR is described,
its size checked,

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.241
then it is followed
until it is ready.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.380
Merging and going to

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.243
production stay in your hands.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.560
Finally, durable
lessons are captured,

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.666
and read back by the next cycle.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.424
The goal: every unit of work

00:01:09.424 --> 00:01:11.075
makes the next one easier.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:14.819
Kaizen.

00:01:14.819 --> 00:01:16.082
For Claude Code.
